{"key":"enterprise/T1567.001","id":"T1567.001","name":"Exfiltration to Code Repository","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1567","tactics":["exfiltration"],"platforms":["ESXi","Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem","virtualization"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may exfiltrate data to a code repository rather than over their primary command and control channel. Code repositories are often accessible via an API (ex: https://api.github.com). Access to these APIs are often over HTTPS, which gives the adversary an additional level of protection. Exfiltration to a code repository can also provide a significant amount of cover to the adversary if it is a popular service already used by hosts…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1567/001","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--86a96bf6-cf8b-411c-aaeb-8959944d64f7","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.686Z","source_object_version":"1.2","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0055","name":"File Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0055","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--235b7491-2d2b-4617-9a52-3c0783680f71","page":"telemetry/DC0055/"},{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0085","name":"Network Traffic Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0085","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3772e279-27d6-477a-9fe3-c6beb363594c","page":"telemetry/DC0085/"},{"id":"DC0078","name":"Network Traffic Flow","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0078","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--a7f22107-02e5-4982-9067-6625d4a1765a","page":"telemetry/DC0078/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0318","name":"Detection Strategy for Exfiltration to Code Repository","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0318","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--ac9c6b7c-bf94-4eeb-926c-f576673c0a14","relationship_id":"relationship--c97fce35-747a-489f-9421-808a69e950a4"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0895","name":"Analytic 0895","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0318#AN0895","guidance":"Processes such as PowerShell, Git, or curl initiating outbound HTTPS POST requests to known code repository APIs (e.g., github.com, gitlab.com) immediately following large file reads. Defender view: correlation between file access of sensitive directories (e.g., Documents, Finance) and abnormal data uploads to repository domains.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0318"},{"id":"AN0896","name":"Analytic 0896","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0318#AN0896","guidance":"Processes like git, curl, or python scripts executing commands that package files (tar, gzip) followed by HTTPS uploads to code repository endpoints. Defender view: detect unusual git push activity or scripted HTTPS requests outside normal developer work hours.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0318"},{"id":"AN0897","name":"Analytic 0897","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0318#AN0897","guidance":"Office or scripting applications initiating unusual HTTPS traffic to code repository APIs with high outbound-to-inbound ratios. Defender perspective: monitor for sensitive file access in combination with network connections to github.com, gitlab.com, or bitbucket.org.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0318"},{"id":"AN0898","name":"Analytic 0898","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0318#AN0898","guidance":"ESXi host processes (vmx, hostd) initiating HTTPS sessions toward external code repositories. Defender perspective: detect datastore reads followed by outbound web traffic inconsistent with administrative baselines.","platforms":["ESXi"],"strategy_id":"DET0318"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0055","component":"File Access","name":"WinEventLog:Security","channel":"EventCode=4663, 4670, 4656","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0895","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0318#AN0895","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0055/"},{"component_id":"DC0082","component":"Network Connection Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=3, 22","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0895","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0318#AN0895","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=1","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0895","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0318#AN0895","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0064","component":"Command Execution","name":"auditd:EXECVE","channel":"git push, curl -X POST","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN0896","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0318#AN0896","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"component_id":"DC0055","component":"File Access","name":"auditd:SYSCALL","channel":"open/read of sensitive directories","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN0896","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0318#AN0896","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telem